  "title": "Nathan I NDE 4440",
  "date": "12 June 1981",
  "content": "It was Independence Day in the Philippines, June 12, 1981. I was only less than six months working at the Philippine National Bank and had just passed the entrance exams at the Ateneo Law School. About 7:00 pm, I was about to cross JP Rizal to the other side of the street to take a ride back because I missed my bus stop. It was drizzling; I had to cover my head with my black jacket. Suddenly, I heard a loud screech of a braking van and before I could react, the van hit me on my side, I was thrown about three meters, and was unconscious. I saw a bright light and had fast flashbacks of the faces of my offices at Philippine National Bank. Then I woke up with people helping me go to the hospital just beside our house at Sta. Ana, the St. Anne's Hospital. I remember that I saw my body on the pavement from above when I was unconscious. When I regained my consciousness, with the help of some people, I was accompanied to the hospital. When the doctor-surgeon arrived, he immediately informed me that I have an internal injury and would have to be opened up immediately otherwise I will die in a short time. I immediately consented to an operation. An exploratory operation was conducted and my spleen was removed as it exploded inside my stomach as a result of the accident.",
